    {
      "id": "q_page4_2",
      "text": "If $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ are the roots of the equation $x^2 + px + 1 = 0$, and $\\gamma, \\delta$ are the roots of the equation $x^2 + qx + 1 = 0$, then $(q^2 - p^2)$ is equal to:",
